title: Who may call this service
subtitle: week-23 - two identical callers, two authorisation layers, one switch that decides whether either is read
width: 1100
---
  CONSUMER VPC  (no NAT, no internet gateway)
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  subnet us-east-1a      subnet us-east-1b    │
  │  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
  │  │   ONE security group, shared           │  │
  │  │                                        │  │
  │  │   client Lambda        intruder Lambda │  │
  │  │   role: orders-client  role: stranger  │  │
  │  │   ── identical code, identical net ──  │  │
  │  └────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
  └───────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
                      │  VPC association (free)
                      ▼
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║  SERVICE NETWORK     authType: AWS_IAM       ║
  ║                                              ║
  ║  auth policy #1  ── this org, this VPC,      ║
  ║                     not anonymous            ║
  ╚═══════════════════┬══════════════════════════╝
                      ▼
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║  SERVICE "rates"     authType: AWS_IAM       ║
  ║                                              ║
  ║  auth policy #2  ── role orders-client,      ║
  ║                     method GET only          ║
  ╚═══════════════════┬══════════════════════════╝
                      ▼
            listener :80  ──▶  target group (LAMBDA)
                                      │
                                      ▼
                            backend Lambda
                            performs NO auth of its own

  BOTH policies must allow. Either authType set to NONE makes its layer
  wave everything through -- while the policy stays attached, stays in the
  console, and reports state: Inactive.
